Description: bound every gh and git call with one shared timeout
Author: Azhou AI Hub
Forwarded: no

Each read path spawned `gh` or `git` and waited for it with no deadline. A call
that hangs, on a stalled network or a credential prompt that never gets answered,
held the whole watch open: no further poll ran and no verdict was ever produced,
and the process was left running until somebody killed it. Every call now shares
one timeout and a call that outlives it is killed and reported as a retryable
timeout, so the watcher goes on polling instead of stalling.

